# Vector Representation and Cosine Similarity

## Overview

This project demonstrates how computers compare the meaning of text using Vector Representation and Cosine Similarity.

Humans can easily understand that words such as "dog" and "puppy" are related, but computers work with numbers rather than language. To enable machines to compare text, sentences are converted into numerical vectors using TF-IDF vectorization.

Cosine Similarity is then used to measure how similar two pieces of text are by comparing the angle between their vectors.

