## Why Plain Text Cannot Be Compared Directly

Computers process numbers, not language.

Text such as:

```text
Dog
Puppy
```

cannot be mathematically compared in raw form.

By converting text into vectors, machine learning algorithms can perform similarity calculations, clustering, classification, and semantic search.

---

## Why Cosine Similarity Uses Angles

Cosine similarity measures the angle between vectors rather than their absolute length.

This is important because:

* Longer sentences naturally contain more words.
* Length alone should not determine similarity.
* Direction represents meaning better than magnitude.

Two sentences discussing the same topic will have vectors pointing in similar directions, producing a higher cosine similarity score.

